<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Ortiz says no budget tricks ahead of poll.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Ortiz says no budget tricks ahead of poll.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican Finance Minister Guillermo Ortiz pledged on Thursday that Mexico will not use budget funds to help the ruling Institutional Revolutionary Party (PRI) win key mid-term elections in July.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no chance that the budget could be used for electoral purposes,&quot; Ortiz told reporters in Mexico City.</p>
<p>Opposition politicians in Mexico charge that the PRI regularly benefits from government funds during election campaigns.</p>
<p>&quot;It does not make sense, because any effort on our part to stimulate the economy in the short-term would have immediate consequences,&quot; Ortiz said.</p>
<p>((--Deborah Montesinos, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9565))</p>
